---
import "../styles/global.css";

const profiles = [
  ["Claude", "Claude", "Claude"],
  ["OpenAI", "OpenAI", "OpenAI"],
  ["Claude/OpenAI", "Claude", "OpenAI"],
  ["OpenAI/Claude", "OpenAI", "Claude"],
];
const modes = [
  ["Quick", "One contained correction", "Conductor direct, no GSD", "Direct verify/fix"],
  ["Feature", "Scoped product change", "A few worktrees", "Loop 1 + integration when needed"],
  ["Project", "Multi-surface work", "Discuss, DAG, waves", "Loop 1, Loop 2, fresh review"],
];
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content="BGSD v2: model-agnostic GSD conductor for Claude Code and Codex." />
    <title>BGSD v2 | Build and verify with the harness you choose</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="nav">
      <a class="brand" href="#top">BGSD <span>v2</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="#contract">Contract</a>
        <a href="#workflow">Workflow</a>
        <a href="#proxy">Proxy</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/filippo-fonseca/better-gsd">GitHub</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main id="top">
      <section class="intro" aria-labelledby="headline">
        <div class="intro-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow">MODEL-AGNOSTIC GSD ORCHESTRATION</p>
          <h1 id="headline">One Conductor.<br />Two independent lanes.</h1>
          <p class="lede">Start in Claude Code or Codex. Quick work stays with the Conductor. Feature and Project work use full GSD build workflows under continuous Conductor steering and fresh evaluation.</p>
          <div class="links">
            <a class="command" href="https://github.com/filippo-fonseca/better-gsd">Read the README <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="quiet-link" href="#proxy">When a proxy helps</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="signal" aria-label="BGSD v2 model contract diagram">
          <div class="signal-banner" aria-label="BGSD pipeline overview"><span>CONDUCT</span><b>PLAN</b><i>BUILD</i><em>VERIFY</em><strong>INTEGRATE</strong></div>
          <div class="signal-grid">
            <article><span>01</span><strong>Conductor</strong><small>Your current Claude Code or Codex session</small></article>
            <article><span>02</span><strong>Build lane</strong><small>Full GSD units, worktrees, repairs</small></article>
            <article><span>03</span><strong>Evaluate lane</strong><small>Loop 1, Loop 2, fresh review</small></article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="contract" class="band">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">THE CONTRACT</p><h2>Conductor reasons. Lanes execute and verify.</h2></div>
        <div class="split">
          <div class="terminal"><div class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><code><span class="muted">$</span> bgsd-sesh<br /><br /><span class="accent">conductor</span>  live session model<br /><span class="green">build</span>      selected subscription lane<br /><span class="orange">evaluate</span>   independent selected lane<br /><br /><span class="muted">routing:</span> fixed | adaptive</code></div>
          <div class="body-copy"><p>The Conductor authors plans, makes routing decisions, and remains the only human-facing agent. It keeps the model and effort of the Claude Code or Codex session you started. Quick implementation stays in that Conductor session. Feature and Project workers receive seeds and a steering directive the Conductor revisits at every phase, commit, blocker, and verification result.</p><p>Pipeline defaults are Claude Opus high for Claude lanes and GPT-5.6 Sol medium for OpenAI lanes. Adaptive routing never guesses: a unit requires an explicit heavy/light assignment and reason. Without one, it runs the profile default. “Heavy” is a routing label, not necessarily high reasoning effort: OpenAI heavy is Sol medium. Model ids are provider-validated, API-key environment variables are scrubbed from child processes, and the direct CLI path uses your existing Claude or ChatGPT subscription.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="profile-table" role="table" aria-label="Pipeline profiles">
          <div class="table-head" role="row"><span>Profile</span><span>Build</span><span>Evaluate</span></div>
          {profiles.map(([profile, build, evaluate]) => <div role="row"><strong>{profile}</strong><span>{build}</span><span>{evaluate}</span></div>)}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="workflow" class="band dark-band">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">WORKFLOW DEPTH</p><h2>The same safety rules at every scale.</h2></div>
        <div class="mode-table" role="table" aria-label="Quick feature project comparison">
          <div class="mode-head" role="row"><span>Mode</span><span>Use it for</span><span>Build</span><span>Evidence</span></div>
          {modes.map(([mode, use, build, evidence]) => <div role="row"><strong>{mode}</strong><span>{use}</span><span>{build}</span><span>{evidence}</span></div>)}
        </div>
        <p class="note">Unit complexity changes GSD phase depth. It does not secretly swap the selected model.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="proxy" class="band proxy-band">
        <div class="section-heading"><p class="eyebrow">OPTIONAL TRANSPORT</p><h2>The proxy is for a different thing.</h2></div>
        <div class="proxy-grid">
          <div><h3>No proxy</h3><p>Claude conducts Codex agents, or Codex conducts Claude agents. BGSD launches the matching CLI directly. This is the normal path.</p></div>
          <div><h3>With CLIProxyAPI</h3><p>You intentionally run the Claude Code harness and tooling while it talks to a GPT model through a local Claude-compatible endpoint.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="guardrail"><span>Guardrail</span><p>Proxy mode is explicit. It requires a local endpoint, token, health probe, and advertised selected model. It does not silently replace direct execution or introduce provider API pricing.</p></div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer><span>BGSD v2</span><span>Direct CLIs by default. Proxy only by choice.</span></footer>
  </body>
</html>
